  "description": "This loft conversion project is based at 31 Chesholm Road N16 0DS London. A couple are seeking to design their loft by adding some space to their existing terrace home. They live in a residential quiet street, a parking permit zone and a few families reside there. The couple seeks to extend their loft and manage what they have for long-term purposes. This project is to fulfill the client’s need for more space to work from home, an additional bedroom to accommodate their children, and to have extended family to visit or stay with. \n \nThe architectural design is to convert their loft to an L-shaped Dormer design, consisting of a bedroom, shower, and workspace. The architecture design will also include project team coordination, M&E, Structural and Fire Safety, etc. The project will erect new interior and exterior walls, and secure a new structural floor and ceiling.",
